title: Red Central Germany
subtitle: The workers hold the copper district and the chemical works.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: march_action = 2 and e21_central_done = 0 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 15
on-arrival: e21_central_done = 1

= Red Central Germany

The police are gone from Mansfeld and Merseburg. [? if e21_march_mode = 2 : Armed workers guard the pitheads, the Leuna gates and the Halle station. The district council meets in the Volkspark, and the Landrat obeys its orders because he has no choice. ?][? if e21_march_mode = 1 : The strike committees have turned into councils, and the councils are in no hurry to dissolve. The managers at Leuna negotiate with them as with a government. ?]

[? if e21_soviet_viable = 1 : Seeckt has told the cabinet that the Reichswehr is not ready for a civil war in Central Germany this spring. ?][? if e21_soviet_viable = 0 : Seeckt has told the cabinet that he can retake the district in a week, if he is given the order. ?]

- @proclaim: Proclaim the Central German Soviet Republic.
- @councils: Keep the councils and the arms, and negotiate.
- @return: Hand back the works and claim the victory.

@proclaim
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] [? if e21_soviet_viable = 1 : The Reichswehr is not ready. ?][? if e21_soviet_viable = 0 : If Seeckt is right, we will stand alone against the army. ?]
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
if (Q.e21_soviet_viable == 1) {
    Q.central_germany_soviet = 2;
    Q.ending_id = 2;
    RG.ecci('zinoviev', 15);
    RG.ecci('bukharin', 15);
    RG.news('Soviet Republic of Central Germany proclaimed in Halle', 3);
    RG.ledger('The Soviet Republic of Central Germany was proclaimed in Halle.', 'e21_cg_soviet');
} else {
    Q.central_germany_soviet = 0;
    for (var d of Q.districts) {
        Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.85;
    }
    RG.district('halle', {repression: 30, guards: -3, members: -0.5});
    Q.red_guards_arms -= 20;
    Q.unity -= 10;
    RG.news('The Reichswehr retakes Halle: the soviet republic lasted eleven days', 3);
    RG.ledger('The Central German soviet republic was crushed by the Reichswehr after eleven days.', 'e21_cg_soviet_crushed');
}
!}

[? if central_germany_soviet = 2 : The council proclaims the Soviet Republic of Central Germany from the steps of the Halle town hall. The Reichswehr gathers on the borders of the province and does not cross them, and Berlin decides that a negotiated frontier is better than a civil war. ?][? if central_germany_soviet = 0 : The proclamation is read on the Halle market square. Five days later the Reichswehr comes from three sides with artillery. The soviet republic lasts eleven days, and the courts are busy for a year afterwards. ?]

- @end: See how it ends.
- @go_on: Continue...

@end
view-if: ending_id = 2
go-to: game_over

@go_on
view-if: ending_id != 2

The party goes on, smaller, and hunted.

@councils
subtitle: Hold what we have won and make the state put it in writing. Halle becomes our fortress.
on-arrival: {!
Q.central_germany_soviet = 1;
RG.district('halle', {repression: -10, guards: 1, loyalty: 15});
Q.stability -= 8;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
RG.ledger('The councils of Halle-Merseburg won recognition from the Prussian government.', 'e21_cg_councils');
!}

The councils stay, the arms stay hidden, and the Prussian government signs an agreement with the district council that it hopes nobody will read too closely. In Central Germany the party is the law in the factories, and the police come only when they are invited.

@return
subtitle: A victory for the whole class. The social democratic workers will remember who gave the works back.
on-arrival: {!
Q.central_germany_soviet = 0;
Q.spd_relation += 8;
Q.worker_support += 6;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
RG.ecci('lenin', 5);
!}

The works are handed back in return for an amnesty and the recognition of the factory councils. In every district the party cannot print membership books fast enough.
